ing, by contrast, is smoothness achieved through completed cycles: lamphron and lamphrodyne exchanging dominance freely, curvature concentrated and then let go, care neither withheld past its season nor spent without renewal. This book has spent twelve chapters insisting that the difference between these two states, a cycle that completes and one that is held, is not a matter of degree but of kind, and it closes by asking the reader to notice which one describes whatever plenum, cognitive, institutional, or otherwise, they themselves currently inhabit.
